<title>UK: Eurobonds - Expected new issues.</title>
<headline>Eurobonds - Expected new issues.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is a summary of expected new issues in the international primary debt market.</p>
<p>The list was compiled from information provided by borrowers, banks mandated to lead manage the issues and other primary market sources. All terms and conditions are indicative.</p>
<p>Details of upcoming bond issues can be telephoned into the London newsroom on +44 171 542 7658</p>
<p>(OFFICIAL indicates confirmed by borrower)</p>
<p>* * * DOLLARS * * *</p>
<p>+ BAYERLB, $1.0 billion 10-year global in June</p>
<p>+ JAPAN DEVELOPMENT BANK, said to be eyeing dollars</p>
<p>+ JAPAN HIGHWAY, considering $500 million 10-year</p>
<p>+ RUSSIA, $1.0 billion, 10 years, J.P. Morgan/SBC Warburg, likely June 18-20(OFFICIAL)</p>
<p>+ TOKYO, seen eyeing dollars</p>
<p>* * * DUTCH GUILDERS * * *</p>
<p>+ AUSTRIA, eyeing sector</p>
<p>+ KREDITANSTALT FUER WEIDERAUFBAU, eyeing sector</p>
<p>* * * FRENCH FRANCS * * *</p>
<p>+ FINLAND, eyeing a deal in French francs for June</p>
<p>+ LVMH, said to be eyeing sector</p>
<p>* * * LIRE * * *</p>
<p>+ BENNETTON GROUP, 500 billion lire</p>
<p>+ FANNIE MAE, considering global bond</p>
<p>* * * MARKS * * *</p>
<p>+ CHINA, 500 million marks in June</p>
<p>+ ESSEN HYPO, global pfandbrief</p>
<p>+ FRANKFURT HYPO, global pfandbrief</p>
<p>+ GERMAN LANDER, said to be planning third Lander jumbo deal</p>
<p>+ ITALY, jumbo marks at five- or seven-years</p>
